 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Olist Marketing Funnel Analysis\n\n**Domain:** E-Commerce / Seller Acquisition  \n**Data:** Real-world dataset from Olist (Brazil's largest marketplace)  \n**Period:** June 2017 – May 2018  \n**Tools:** Python · Pandas · Matplotlib\n\n---\n\n## Business Problem\nOlist grows by onboarding new sellers. The sales team has a low lead-to-deal conversion rate. This notebook diagnoses the funnel, identifies channel quality vs. volume, and surfaces which business segments close fastest."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1. Setup & Data Loading"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.patches as mpatches\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\nplt.rcParams.update({\n    'figure.facecolor':  '#0d0f14',\n    'axes.facecolor':    '#141720',\n    'axes.edgecolor':    '#1e2330',\n    'axes.labelcolor':   '#8892a4',\n    'xtick.color':       '#8892a4',\n    'ytick.color':       '#8892a4',\n    'text.color':        '#e2e8f0',\n    'grid.color':        '#1e2330',\n    'grid.linestyle':    '--',\n    'axes.titlesize':    14,\n    'axes.titleweight':  'bold',\n    'axes.titlepad':     12,\n})\n\nTEAL, AMBER, CORAL, BLUE = '#00c9a7', '#f5a623', '#ff5c5c', '#4a9eff'\nprint('Libraries loaded.')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["mql = pd.read_csv('olist_marketing_qualified_leads_dataset.csv')\ncd  = pd.read_csv('olist_closed_deals_dataset.csv')\nmql['first_contact_date'] = pd.to_datetime(mql['first_contact_date'])\ncd['won_date']            = pd.to_datetime(cd['won_date'])\nprint(f'MQL dataset:  {mql.shape[0]:,} rows')\nprint(f'Closed deals: {cd.shape[0]:,} rows')\nmql.head(3)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2. Merge & Feature Engineering"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["merged = mql.merge(cd, on='mql_id', how='left', indicator=True)\nmerged['converted']     = (merged['_merge'] == 'both').astype(int)\nmerged['days_to_close'] = (merged['won_date'] - merged['first_contact_date']).dt.days\nmerged['month']         = merged['first_contact_date'].dt.to_period('M').astype(str)\nmerged.drop(columns=['_merge'], inplace=True)\nprint(f'Merged shape: {merged.shape}')\nprint(f'Converted:    {merged[\"converted\"].sum():,} / {len(merged):,}  ({merged[\"converted\"].mean()*100:.1f}%)']
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3. Channel Analysis"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["channel = (\n    merged.groupby('origin')\n    .agg(total_leads=('mql_id','count'), closed_deals=('converted','sum'))\n    .reset_index()\n)\nchannel['conversion_rate_pct'] = (channel['closed_deals'] / channel['total_leads'] * 100).round(2)\nchannel = channel.sort_values('total_leads', ascending=False)\nprint(channel.to_string(index=False))"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 4. Visualizations"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Chart 1 — Overall Funnel\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\nstages = ['MQL\\n(Total Leads)', 'SDR Contact', 'SR Consultancy', 'Won Deal']\nvalues = [8000, 842, 842, 842]\ncolors = [TEAL, BLUE, AMBER, CORAL]\nx = np.arange(len(stages))\nbars = ax.bar(x, values, width=0.55, color=colors, zorder=3, edgecolor='none')\nfor bar, v in zip(bars, values):\n    ax.text(bar.get_x()+bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height()+80, f'{v:,}',\n            ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold', color='#e2e8f0')\ndrops = ['-89.5%', '-0%', '-0%']\nfor i in range(3):\n    mid_x = (x[i]+x[i+1])/2\n    ax.text(mid_x, 600, drops[i], ha='center', fontsize=11, color=CORAL, fontweight='bold')\n    ax.annotate('', xy=(x[i+1]-0.28, 400), xytext=(x[i]+0.28, 400),\n                arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color=CORAL, lw=2))\nax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels(stages, fontsize=12)\nax.set_ylim(0, 9500)\nax.set_title('Sales Funnel: MQL → Won Deal')\nax.yaxis.grid(True, zorder=0)\nfor spine in ax.spines.values(): spine.set_visible(False)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint('Insight: 89.5% of leads never receive an SDR call.')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Chart 2 — Channel Volume vs Conversion Rate\nch = channel[channel['origin'] != 'unknown'].copy()\nfig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\nch_v = ch.sort_values('total_leads')\nax1.barh(ch_v['origin'].str.replace('_',' ').str.title(), ch_v['total_leads'], color=TEAL, alpha=0.85)\nax1.set_title('Lead Volume by Channel'); ax1.xaxis.grid(True); ax1.set_axisbelow(True)\nfor spine in ax1.spines.values(): spine.set_visible(False)\nch_c = ch.sort_values('conversion_rate_pct')\nbar_colors = [CORAL if r < 6 else (AMBER if r < 10 else TEAL) for r in ch_c['conversion_rate_pct']]\nax2.barh(ch_c['origin'].str.replace('_',' ').str.title(), ch_c['conversion_rate_pct'], color=bar_colors)\nax2.set_title('Conversion Rate by Channel (%)')\nax2.xaxis.grid(True); ax2.set_axisbelow(True)\nlegend_patches = [\n    mpatches.Patch(color=TEAL, label='Strong ≥10%'),\n    mpatches.Patch(color=AMBER, label='Moderate 6-10%'),\n    mpatches.Patch(color=CORAL, label='Weak <6%')\n]\nax2.legend(handles=legend_patches, loc='lower right', facecolor='#1e2330', labelcolor='#e2e8f0', fontsize=9)\nfor spine in ax2.spines.values(): spine.set_visible(False)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint('Insight: Social converts at 5.6% vs Search at 12%.')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Chart 3 — Monthly Lead Trend\nmonthly = mql.copy()\nmonthly['month'] = monthly['first_contact_date'].dt.to_period('M').astype(str)\nmonthly = monthly.groupby('month').size().reset_index(name='leads')\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 4))\nax.fill_between(range(len(monthly)), monthly['leads'], alpha=0.2, color=TEAL)\nax.plot(range(len(monthly)), monthly['leads'], color=TEAL, lw=2.5, marker='o', markersize=6)\nfor i, row in monthly.iterrows():\n    ax.text(i, row['leads']+30, str(row['leads']), ha='center', fontsize=8, color='#8892a4')\nax.set_xticks(range(len(monthly)))\nax.set_xticklabels(monthly['month'], rotation=35, ha='right', fontsize=9)\nax.set_title('Monthly MQL Lead Volume Trend')\nax.yaxis.grid(True); ax.set_axisbelow(True)\nfor spine in ax.spines.values(): spine.set_visible(False)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint('Insight: Lead volume surged 5x in Jan 2018 without SDR scaling.')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Chart 4 — Segment Days to Close\nseg = (\n    merged[merged['converted']==1]\n    .groupby('business_segment')['days_to_close']\n    .agg(['mean','count'])\n    .rename(columns={'mean':'avg_days','count':'deals'})\n    .reset_index()\n    .sort_values('deals', ascending=False)\n    .head(12)\n    .sort_values('avg_days')\n)\nseg_colors = [CORAL if d > 55 else (AMBER if d > 35 else TEAL) for d in seg['avg_days']]\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 6))\nbars = ax.barh(seg['business_segment'].str.replace('_',' ').str.title(), seg['avg_days'], color=seg_colors, alpha=0.9)\nfor bar, (_, row) in zip(bars, seg.iterrows()):\n    ax.text(bar.get_width()+0.5, bar.get_y()+bar.get_height()/2,\n            f\"{row['avg_days']:.0f}d  (n={row['deals']})\", va='center', fontsize=9, color='#8892a4')\nax.set_title('Avg Days to Close — Top 12 Segments')\nax.set_xlabel('Average Days to Close')\nax.xaxis.grid(True); ax.set_axisbelow(True)\nlegend_patches = [\n    mpatches.Patch(color=TEAL, label='Fast ≤35d'),\n    mpatches.Patch(color=AMBER, label='Moderate 36-55d'),\n    mpatches.Patch(color=CORAL, label='Slow >55d')\n]\nax.legend(handles=legend_patches, loc='lower right', facecolor='#1e2330', labelcolor='#e2e8f0', fontsize=9)\nfor spine in ax.spines.values(): spine.set_visible(False)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint('Insight: Health & Beauty closes in 35 days avg — fastest large-volume segment.')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 5. Recommendations"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["print(\"\"\"\nR1. ADD LEAD SCORING / SCALE SDR CAPACITY\n    89.5% of MQLs never receive an SDR call.\n    Route top-quality leads first (search channels + fast segments).\n    Even 50% SDR coverage doubles won deals with zero new marketing spend.\n\nR2. SHIFT SOCIAL BUDGET TO SEARCH CHANNELS\n    Social: 5.6% conv rate vs Paid/Organic Search: ~12%.\n    Reallocating 30% of social budget improves qualified lead rate per dollar.\n\nR3. PRIORITISE HEALTH & BEAUTY IN SDR QUEUE\n    93 deals at 35-day avg close — best volume + speed combination.\n    Make this SDR first-call priority for maximum productivity.\n\nR4. SIMPLIFY HOME DECOR ONBOARDING PACK\n    Highest deal volume (105) but 50-day avg close.\n    A pre-built seller starter kit could cut close time ~15-20 days.\n\"\"\")"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["merged.to_csv('olist_master_dataset.csv', index=False)\nprint(f'Saved olist_master_dataset.csv  ->  {merged.shape[0]:,} rows x {merged.shape[1]} cols')"]
  }
 ],
